= The Trial of Max Hoelz

Max Hoelz was caught in Berlin this spring, living under a false name. Before the special court in Moabit he does not defend himself. He accuses: the prisoners beaten and shot in March, the Kapp officers who were never tried, the hunger in the Vogtland.

On 22 June he is sentenced to penal servitude for life for the killing of a landowner, a killing he almost certainly did not commit. The public gallery sings the Internationale as he is taken down.

- @campaign: Make him the face of the March prisoners.
- @relief: Build Red Aid for all the prisoners.
- @distance: Keep our distance from a bank robber.

@campaign
subtitle: Popular in Saxony and the Vogtland, and a cause that will outlast the year.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_hoelz_campaign = 1;
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 6, loyalty: 4});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

"Free Max Hoelz" is painted on walls from Plauen to Hamburg.

@relief
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Lawyers, parcels and money for the families. Slow work, and it keeps members.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.unity += 4;
RG.district('halle', {loyalty: 8});
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Red Aid committees form in every district. Many of the families they help are not communists. Some of them become communists.

@distance
subtitle: Respectable. Central Germany will not like it.
on-arrival: spd_relation += 3; district_halle_loyalty -= 6; district_saxony_loyalty -= 6

The Rote Fahne reports the sentence in a short notice on page three.
